A||||46||Sleeper||West Coast Fiero Cold Air-Intake pics||||14||
Z||000000||Sleeper||04-01-2001||02:52 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Apr01$01_2.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Apr01$02_1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Apr01$03_3.jpg">  <BR>first time with PIP, hope it works<P>finally, geez, well anyways, the car is qucker/faster. the rpm's go up slower but the car accelerates faster than stock so i'm getting more out of the gear.i have an auto tranny but stick might be the same<P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero custom Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, J.E.T. super chip, MSD Blaster Coil, and Optima Battery.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Seanh||04-01-2001||03:22 PM||||That looks cool, but I must ask, whats the advantage over the stock air-intake setup? It looks like it pull air from the same place, so what makes it worth it? I looked into getting one, but really couldn't see the advantage in it.<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sleeper||04-01-2001||03:31 PM||||when i pulled out the stock intake system i noticed that there were alot of restrictions the incoming air has to go through to get to the motor. these aftermarket intakes are free flowing/no restrictions and you can hear it too, its loud. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TwisT||04-01-2001||04:14 PM||||Nice!<P>I notice the air-filter isn't a K&N...  do they give you the option?<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||04-01-2001||04:24 PM||||Actually, despite the looks of the stock intake, it's remarkably well designed.  And it's also a true cold-air intake - it's sealed off from the engine compartment, unlike this one.  And there's nothing to stop that HKS filter from getting sopping wet...<P>With a better flowing intake the engine should rev quicker, not slower... and before you say it's quicker, take it to the strip and/or dyno.  The ass-o-meter isn't that finely calibrated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||04-01-2001||05:27 PM||||How hard would it be to redo the stock intake system and remove all the restrictions? Run new straight pipe and perhaps a different air filter.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Taijiguy||04-01-2001||05:35 PM||||All those restrictions are by design, and primarily help to keep the noise down, as well as make sure the air coming in is dry. I think those aftermarket cold air intakes are just alot more work. I think you'll be cleaning that filter a LOT. It's different though. How about that bar that connects the strut towers, any real effect from that?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||c m west||04-01-2001||05:46 PM||||ever notice that those who have our products dont complain, and those that dont just speculate - until they step up to our add on - nothing we make here is a gimmick ( with the exeption of the strut tower brace - but hey, it looks cool )<P> Craig choose to go with the HKS filter cause he wanted to - thats cool. We go with the extreme series K&N, but didnt have them in yet - Pro-Motion is really dicking us around lately and I dont appreciate it - the filters were supposed to be here a week ago - Im gonna have to go down there and wrap a tire iron around there neck, cause there being jerky little rubba-necks <P> But in any case, were here to work with people who want something rare or different for there car, were based around custom fabrication - that intake has been on the market for 2 years now - with absolutly no problems, if you dont want air to get into - then dont drive into a lake - there is not enough volumetric effiency, let alone vacum pressure for the motor to be sucking in water from a vent a foot and a half off the ground<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<p>[This message has been edited by c m west (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||c m west||04-01-2001||05:57 PM||||Craig - drop on by today so we can presseure wash you engine bay - PLEASE.... hehehehe<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000009||Sleeper||04-01-2001||07:51 PM||||yea i know Eric it looked like sh*t, i cleaned it up already. all that black material around the engine was a bi*ch to put out but i'm glad i did it cuz that crap keeps the heat in.<P>please tell me how the filter is gonna get wet?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> 1)look from the top, the filter is down in the hole so no water from up top 2)i still have my inside fenders(or whatever you wanna call them) on so no water from the tires 3) the filter is like 2 or 2 & half feet from the ground so no water spashing up from the ground plus the groundFX on the sides go in to block most of the water spashing up.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>anything else you'd like to TRY and clown me on?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> just cuz i got the COOL GUY west coast fiero cold air intake and the COOL GUY strut tower bar.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>and Eric i think i forgot my <B>key lock</B> for my rims at your shop last month when you lowered my car, if you have time can you look through your tools, if not i'll just buy a new one or two.<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
