Z||000011||Shaun41178||04-01-2001||08:55 PM||||Like standard said if you say your car is faster then the it should rev faster too.  If it revved slower then it would accelerate slower.  Think about it.  Also I don't think you can feel a real difference in acceleration with an intake.  +5 hp it makes most likely at a high rpm.  You won't feel that hp trust me.  I have a cold air setup on mine and dynoed +2 peak.  Can't feel it.  Dyno could tell though.  Dyno the stock and the WESt coast one and see what it really makes.||||reg||1
