Z||000041||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||11:39 AM||||you can remove more useless parts too if you bored... the area i marked in yellow (1) there are 2 10mm screws that hold this resonator and the ambient air feed to the EGR solenoid. you can pull the one screw from the fire wall near the throttle body and the other near the wiring harness on the passengerside just to the left of the hood hinge. and (2) the throttle body coolant line can come out.<BR>-i wrote how to bypass the TB coolant lines... - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009196.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009196.html</A> <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sleeperintake.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
